docs/operators.md:178:## Hosted External Project Deployment First Slice
docs/operators.md:179:
docs/operators.md:180:Port now has one bounded answer to "can it host an external project?" without
docs/operators.md:181:claiming a general hosted platform or a container-like app bundle surface.
docs/operators.md:182:
docs/operators.md:183:Review surface:
docs/operators.md:184:
docs/operators.md:185:```bash
docs/operators.md:186:just mission
docs/operators.md:187:```
docs/operators.md:188:
docs/operators.md:189:Runnable hosted workflow:
docs/operators.md:190:
docs/operators.md:191:```bash
docs/operators.md:192:bash scripts/hosted-external-project-demo.sh
docs/operators.md:193:```
docs/operators.md:194:
docs/operators.md:195:That proof path keeps the operator contract explicit:
docs/operators.md:196:
docs/operators.md:197:- repo-local hosted control plane plus node agent
docs/operators.md:198:- one hosted machine: `cloud-aws`
docs/operators.md:199:- one explicit host group: `aws-builders`
docs/operators.md:200:- one repo-local external static-site snapshot:
docs/operators.md:201:  `examples/external-static-site/index.html`
docs/operators.md:202:- one staging path through hosted `port guest copy`
docs/operators.md:203:- one minimal HTTP service launched through `port service apply`
docs/operators.md:204:- one host-side exposure through `port guest forward`
docs/operators.md:205:- one host-side `curl` proving the payload
docs/operators.md:206:
docs/operators.md:207:Human-reviewable artifact:
docs/operators.md:208:
docs/operators.md:209:```bash
docs/operators.md:210:./scripts/render-external-project-proof.sh .keel/stories/VEyjdN0nf/EVIDENCE
docs/operators.md:211:```
docs/operators.md:212:
docs/operators.md:213:The current proof prerequisites are intentionally narrow:
docs/operators.md:214:
docs/operators.md:215:- run from the repo dev shell so `port`, `port-guest-agent`, `busybox`, `curl`,
docs/operators.md:216:  and `agg` are available
docs/operators.md:217:- keep `PORT_DEMO_TOKEN` available for the repo-local hosted control-plane
docs/operators.md:218:  contract, or rely on the script's repo-default `demo-token`
